<section class="section" id="overview"><span class="orb left"></span><div class="container">
<div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Product overview</div><h2>Less friction.<br><em>More saved moments.</em></h2></div><p>SaveIt is presented as a single place to start a download, choose the right quality, track active tasks and revisit saved media without jumping between disconnected screens.</p></div>
<div class="overview-grid"><div class="overview-copy reveal"><h3>Make content saving feel <span class="serif accent">effortless.</span></h3><p>The supplied interface concept has a clear, task-led structure: a home screen for pasting a link, popular platform shortcuts, a quality-selection step, a download queue, a saved-content library and a settings area.</p><p>The design story focuses on understandable actions and visible status. Users should know what they can save, which quality they selected, how far a task has progressed and where a completed file can be found.</p></div>
<div class="stat-grid reveal delay-1"><div class="stat"><div class="num">01</div><strong>Paste a link</strong><p>Start with a familiar, focused input and a clear download action.</p></div><div class="stat"><div class="num">02</div><strong>Choose quality</strong><p>Review format, resolution and estimated file size before saving.</p></div><div class="stat"><div class="num">03</div><strong>Track progress</strong><p>See progress, speed, queued tasks and cancellation controls.</p></div><div class="stat"><div class="num">04</div><strong>Manage media</strong><p>Browse saved videos, photos and audio from one library.</p></div></div></div>
<div class="capability-strip reveal"><div class="capability"><span class="symbol">↧</span><div><b>Link-first flow</b><small>Paste and begin in a few steps</small></div></div><div class="capability"><span class="symbol">◷</span><div><b>Visible progress</b><small>Active and queued download states</small></div></div><div class="capability"><span class="symbol">▤</span><div><b>Media library</b><small>Saved files organised by type</small></div></div><div class="capability"><span class="symbol">◇</span><div><b>Room to scale</b><small>Premium and utility feature concepts</small></div></div></div>
</div></section>

