<div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Application architecture</div><h2>From tap to<br><em>completed download.</em></h2></div><p>A conceptual architecture map communicates how a cross-platform client can separate the interface, workflow coordination, download processing and local media management.</p></div>
<div class="architecture reveal"><div class="architecture-top"><h3>Suggested application architecture</h3><small>CONCEPTUAL SYSTEM VIEW</small></div><div class="arch-tree">
<div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">▣</span><div><b>Presentation layer</b><small>Flutter screens · reusable widgets · navigation · forms</small></div><em>01 / UI</em></div><div class="arch-connector"></div>
<div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">⌘</span><div><b>State &amp; workflow management</b><small>Input validation · loading states · task status · error feedback</small></div><em>02 / STATE</em></div><div class="arch-connector"></div>
<div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">◇</span><div><b>Download orchestration</b><small>Link validation · metadata lookup · format and quality selection</small></div><em>03 / DOMAIN</em></div><div class="arch-connector"></div>
<div class="arch-node"><span class="arch-icon">⇄</span><div><b>Repository / service adapters</b><small>Download provider integration · file handling · persistence boundaries</small></div><em>04 / DATA</em></div><div class="arch-connector"></div>
