<section class="section" id="principles"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Core engineering concepts</div><h2>The craft behind<br><em>the simple flow.</em></h2></div><p>A polished utility app needs reliable task handling and clear feedback as much as it needs attractive screens.</p></div>
<div class="concept-grid">
<article class="concept-card reveal"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">▦</span><span>CORE 01</span></div><h3>Reusable design system</h3><p>Consistent cards, input fields, quality rows, progress indicators and navigation patterns keep the product coherent.</p></article>
<article class="concept-card reveal delay-1"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⌘</span><span>CORE 02</span></div><h3>Explicit task states</h3><p>Represent queued, preparing, downloading, completed, cancelled and failed states instead of relying on ambiguous spinners.</p></article>
<article class="concept-card reveal delay-2"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⇄</span><span>CORE 03</span></div><h3>Service boundaries</h3><p>Separate UI concerns from metadata resolution, download execution, file operations and persistence.</p></article>
<article class="concept-card reveal"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">✓</span><span>CORE 04</span></div><h3>Permission handling</h3><p>Request device permissions only when needed and provide useful recovery guidance when access is denied.</p></article>
<article class="concept-card reveal delay-1"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">◷</span><span>CORE 05</span></div><h3>Background resilience</h3><p>Plan for interruptions, connectivity changes, retries, duplicate tasks and app lifecycle transitions.</p></article>
<article class="concept-card reveal delay-2"><div class="concept-top"><span class="concept-icon">⌁</span><span>CORE 06</span></div><h3>Privacy by design</h3><p>Store only necessary data, explain file permissions and avoid exposing source URLs or account details unnecessarily.</p></article>
</div></div></section>

